Supposedly, the proper way to shoot arrows is to wield the bow, then throw
the arrow.  I'd been playing like that for years. (On 2.3 etc.)

Well, the guy who played with the xan and the stethoscope is right!
Arrows always do lame damage no matter what propeller you use, and throwing
a bow does the desired damage!

The fix should go in dmgval(obj, mdat) in weapon.c.

I'm working on it now.  If you have wizard mode, try it out.  You're much
better off throwing bows!!!!  Print tmp in hmon() in uhitm.c if you do
not believe me. E-mail me if you already made a good fix, or if you want mine.

